                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1011: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-06T13:00:00-06:00">December 6, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. The Commission is considering eliminating point number 6 (stamps) on the
                    insistence of Honduras. I have not yet agreed to this and would appreciate the
                    Department’s telegraphic instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
